{title: Holy God, We Praise Thy Name}
{artist: Ignaz Franz (1771); tr. Clarence A. Walworth (1853)}
{key: F}
{tempo: 88}
{time: 3/4}
{meta: tune GROSSER GOTT - Katholisches Gesangbuch, Vienna (1774)}
{meta: public_domain Text 1853, tune 1774: both published before 1931 (US public domain); all authors, translators and composers died over 70 years ago. Chords and section layout: original simple arrangement by Tabernacle Tools. Original verses only, no modern additions.}

{start_of_verse: Verse 1}
[F]Holy God, we [C]praise Thy [F]name; Lord of all, we [C]bow be[F]fore Thee!
[F]All on earth Thy [C]scepter [F]claim, all in heaven a[C]bove a[F]dore Thee;
[C]Infinite Thy [F]vast do[C]main, [F]everlasting [Bb]is Thy [C]reign.
[C]Infinite Thy [F]vast do[C]main, [F]everlasting [C]is Thy [F]reign.
{end_of_verse}
{start_of_verse: Verse 2}
[F]Hark! the loud ce[C]lestial [F]hymn angel choirs a[C]bove are [F]raising,
[F]Cherubim and [C]seraph[F]im, in unceasing [C]chorus [F]praising;
[C]Fill the heavens with [F]sweet ac[C]cord: [F]Holy, holy, [Bb]holy [C]Lord.
[C]Fill the heavens with [F]sweet ac[C]cord: [F]Holy, holy, [C]holy [F]Lord.
{end_of_verse}
